questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue involving a multi-threaded data pipeline. The following service was designed to initialize a shared resource lazily without global synchronization on every read:

java
@Component
public class ConfigurationRegistry {
    private Map<String, String> runtimeConfig;
    private boolean initialized = false;

    public void loadConfiguration(Map<String, String> configs) {
        this.runtimeConfig = new HashMap<>(configs);
        this.initialized = true;
    }

    public String getProperty(String key) {
        if (!initialized) {
            return null;
        }
        return runtimeConfig.get(key);
    }
}


Under high concurrency, worker threads occasionally throw a `NullPointerException` inside `runtimeConfig.get(key)`, or retrieve `null` even though the key was guaranteed to be present in `configs`.
